(503, 10, NULL, 1, 'remotive', 'https://remotive.com/remote-jobs/communications/communications-manager-2090985', NULL, 'Communications Manager', 'Communications', 'Lemon.io', 'own_company', NULL, 'visible', 'LATAM, Europe', 'About Lemon.ioLemon.io is building the autopilot for hiring. We\'ve replaced the slow, expensive recruiting agency with a platform that delivers vetted, responsive candidates, ready for a final interview. In days, not weeks. Hundreds of fast-growing companies use Lemon to build their engineering teams, from early-stage startups to enterprises. We\'re profitable, bootstrapped, and growing at a moment when the legacy recruiting industry is being rewritten in real time.Here\'s why this role exists. We have a great story and almost no one telling it. A profitable company helping rewrite a huge industry with AI, and a voice that is still a blank canvas. You\'d be the one who decides how Lemon sounds and makes the market pay attention, working directly with the founder, with the freedom that comes from being bootstrapped.About the positionThe Communications Manager will own Lemon\'s external voice and its distribution.The goal: make Lemon impossible to ignore in the engineering-hiring conversation. Every day, something from Lemon should be visible where our buyers and candidates already are, until the market treats us as the category leader.This is a senior IC role, reporting directly to the founder. You\'ll personally do most of the writing and build systems for distribution.This is an intensive role. You\'ll be producing daily and running a content distribution engine that doesn\'t stop. And while we\'d typically expect 4+ years of experience, we\'re genuinely open to less experienced candidates who can demonstrate exceptional writing and judgment.Responsibilities:1. Executive Communications- Lead the creation and execution of founders\' personal brand platforms- Produce and distribute day-to-day content across founders\' channels- Support founders\' earned media: podcasts, panels, op-eds, and speaking opportunities2. Internal News Scouting and Narrative Development- Sit in product, customer success, sales, and ops syncs to identify newsworthy stories- Identify and shape company moments worth telling publicly- Translate internal milestones, launches, learnings, and customer wins into external content- Distribute content via social and traditional media.3. Team Engagement- Build and support an internal content program that engages employees across functions- Equip team members to share their work publicly through ready-to-use content and templates- Coordinate the team\'s participation in industry conversations across channels4. Monitoring, Automation- Build and maintain content and distribution workflows using AI tools- Set up monitoring for brand mentions, press coverage, and audience growth across channels- Track, grow and report on key communications metrics quarterlyWhat we\'re looking for:- Native or fluent English with cultural fluency for the US tech audience- A genuinely strong writer. - You\'ve been the voice behind someone else\'s posts. - Track record telling the story of a company, a product, or a movement- Background in technology, B2B software, talent, recruiting, dev tools, or adjacent industries.- You’re deeply immersed in the world of independent media: Substackers, podcasters, influencers on X or LinkedIn. - AI is already part of how you work.- Comfortable operating in areas of genuine uncertainty.- Results-oriented, with a bias toward action and impact.- Want to be part of a small, fast-paced, and impactful team.What success looks like in the first 4 weeks:- You\'ve built systems to capture content from our team and product, and to manufacture news.- You\'ve launched an amplification program by the team and outside voices, so every message travels.- A repurposing workflow exists: one idea becomes a post, a thread, a clip, a newsletter line, without starting over each time.- You\'ve identified the 3 to 5 narratives that everyone will repeat.- You\'ve identified a few internal voices and enabled them to post regularly, with systems that feed them content ideas.- By week 4, the founder\'s social posts go out 4 to 5 times a week.- Baseline metrics captured, so growth is measurable from a known starting point.Application ProcessTo apply, send us:- Three writing samples that show range. At least one should be in a voice that isn\'t yours: something you ghost-wrote for an executive, a founder, or another public-facing operator. - A short note (200 words or fewer) telling us why this role and what you\'d want to ship in your first 90 days. The point isn\'t to summarize your resume. It\'s to give us a sense of how you think and what you\'d actually do.What to expect:- Application review within 7 days- 45-minute call with the hiring team- Paid trial project (up to 10 hours)- Final 60-minute conversation with the founder- Reference checks and offerWe aim to move from application to offer within 3-4 weeks.', 'go, AI/ML, automation, responsive', 'Not specified', 1, 0, 'OFF', 'open', '2026-07-04 11:49:07', 'full_time', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
(504, 10, NULL, 1, 'remotive', 'https://remotive.com/remote-jobs/customer-service/client-success-coach-csm-2091039', NULL, 'Client Success Coach (CSM)', 'Customer Service', 'Impact Clients', 'own_company', NULL, 'visible', 'Northern America, Europe, South Africa', 'We’re looking for a full-time Client Success Coach to join our fast-growing team at Richard Yu’s online education company. Our mission is simple: help everyday people launch impactful online digital arbitrage businesses that transform lives—starting with their own.If you’re someone who loves mentorship, thrives in a high-performance environment, and wants to make a real difference in people’s lives, keep reading.About Us:Richard Yu is an online business coach with: 100K+ subscribers on YouTube → youtube.com/richardyu1 A growing personal brand on Instagram → instagram.com/richardyuzee Our company is fast-paced, and rooted in service. We’re building a world-class education platform to help people turn their knowledge into income through coaching and consulting.About The Role:This is a remote, full-time position. You must be available during 8AM–5PM EST, Monday to Friday. On average, you’ll work up to 9 hours per day, and some days will require a little more effort of 10 hours.You must currently live in North America, Europe, or South Africa, and speak fluent, accent-neutral English. Clear communication is non-negotiable, we’re in the coaching business. Requirements Here are the requirements: You must be able to commit full time hours (Our office hours are 9 AM - 6 PM EST, though if you are different time zones we\'re super open minded) You will be conducting new onboarding calls daily to welcome in new students. You will be conducting check in coaching calls daily, to hold accountable, motivate, and inspire students inside the program (must be comfortable jumping on 1:1 Zoom calls or recording Loom videos as needed. You will be messaging clients on a daily basis, in order to hold them accountable to their plan of execution towards their goals and moderating the community. Weekly group coaching calls answering client questions Must have strong communication/interpersonal skills so we can put you in front of our clients and you can confidently answer their questions and guide their decisions Help innovate our products by creating and producing new video trainings/worksheets to deliver a world-class experience. Taking renewal / upgrade calls with clients and enrolling them into our backend coaching programs. Should be proficient or at least knowledgeable about our tech stack (Loom, ActiveCampaign, Slack, Zapier, Calendly, GSuite, CRM, etc.) - you should be familiar with the above tools, or have a willingness to learn these VERY quickly if hired. Your role will constantly be changing. A big part of this job is to stay on your toes, always ready for action and change. You will be responsible for daily reporting on multiple communication channels (Slack, text message, spreadsheets, etc.,) and so a high attention to detail and compliance with standard operating procedures is essential. You must have a high attention to detail and understand systems/processes so you are able to innovate new, more efficient SOPs (processes) to ensure our Fulfillment Team hits their KPIs WHO THIS IS FOR: A coach or mentor at heart—you love helping people Clear, professional communicator (spoken and written English) Experienced with organic marketing on Instagram/Facebook/TikTok (creating reels, organic posts, to generate organic leads) Sales background Able to handle fast-paced environments, multiple clients, and changing priorities Willing to grow with us long-term (3+ years)—this isn’t a side hustle Open to feedback and constructive coaching (we’ll train you, but we expect growth) Comfortable with tools like Loom, Calendly, Slack, GSuite, CRMs, etc—or willing to learn fast WHO THIS IS NOT FOR: You have another full-time job or multiple freelance clients You struggle with structure, deadlines, or fast execution You dislike being challenged to improve daily Benefits Expected Earnings (Rev share on book of business): $10,000–$15,000+ USD/month (depending on experience) Commission opportunities: % on referrals, upgrades, renewals, and pending payment collections.', 'backend, video, CRM, youtube, organic marketing, onboarding, spreadsheets, gsuite', 'Not specified', 1, 0, 'OFF', 'open', '2026-07-04 11:49:07', 'full_time', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL),
(505, 10, NULL, 1, 'remotive', 'https://remotive.com/remote-jobs/sales/sales-assistant-2091038', NULL, 'Sales Assistant', 'Sales', 'Endureed by Global Innovation', 'own_company', NULL, 'visible', 'USA', 'This role may require you to be on site at times - please check with the employer first. Job Title: Sales Assistant Company: Endureed Location: Lake City, FL / Remote eligible Reports to: VP of Global Sales ABOUT THE ROLE The Sales Assistant is the operational backbone of the US sales team. You\'ll provide hands-on administrative, coordination, and customer support to the VP of Global Sales — keeping the department running smoothly, accurately, and on time across residential and Strategic Partner (SP) channels. This isn\'t a role for someone who wants to wing it, work independently without structure, or stay at arm\'s length from the details. It\'s a role for someone who finds real satisfaction in making sure nothing falls through the cracks someone who takes pride in accuracy, follows through without being asked twice, and genuinely enjoys being the person others can count on. If you\'re the kind of person who gets energized by creating order, supporting a team, and doing the unglamorous-but-critical work that makes everything else possible keep reading. ✓ You\'ll thrive here if you... • Get genuine satisfaction from organizing, tracking, and keeping things accurate • Take ownership of tasks and follow through without being reminded • Prefer a defined role with clear expectations over open-ended autonomy • Are naturally calm, steady, and don\'t rattle easily when things get busy • Build trust by being dependable, not by being loud • Take pride in serving others and helping your team look good • Are bilingual in English and Spanish and comfortable using both professionally • Thrive in a structured, process-driven environment with consistent routines ✗ This role is NOT for you if you... • Need to be the center of attention or get credit to feel motivated • Prefer creating your own process over following an established one • Dislike repetitive tasks or detailed administrative work • Get bored or frustrated when you\'re not driving strategy or making big decisions • Struggle to stay organized when managing multiple people\'s priorities at once • Want flexibility to define your own schedule or work style without check-ins • Move fast and loose, accuracy and follow-through aren\'t your strong suits • Are looking for a stepping stone to a sales rep role as fast as possible KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Day-to-day, you will: • Provide administrative support to the VP of Global Sales, calendar management, scheduling, travel coordination, and communications • Prepare and update sales reports, presentations, and customer-facing materials for residential and SP accounts • Own CRM data entry, lead tracking, and pipeline management, data must be accurate and current at all times • Coordinate between the sales team and the SP network, including onboarding new partners and managing ongoing communication • Track SP territory coverage and ensure Basics product line distribution aligns with current SP network policies • Conduct market and competitor research to support US sales strategy • Help organize sales campaigns, trade shows, events, and client meetings, logistics, materials, follow-up • Ensure timely document and information flow between the sales team, operations, and other departments • Support order processing and client onboarding across residential and SP channels WHAT YOU BRING • Bilingual — English and Spanish required, written and spoken (non-negotiable) • 2+ years in a sales support, coordinator, or administrative role, you\'ve done this before and you\'re good at it • CRM experience required; NetSuite or similar ERP a strong plus • Proficiency with Microsoft Office and/or Google Workspace, especially Excel/Sheets and PowerPoint/Slides • Exceptional organizational skills, you manage multiple moving pieces without losing track of any of them • High attention to detail, errors bother you before anyone else catches them • Calm, professional communication style, written and verbal • Experience in building materials, construction, or a product-based industry is a plus, not a requirement To apply, please complete our Culture Index survey before submitting your application: https://go.cultureindex.com/p/dmxXuQJk6Y4WKDaTvN Applications without a completed survey will not be considered. Send an email to careers@endureed.com with the subject line: \"Sales Assistant Application, First and Last Name\" (replace with your name)', 'research, CRM, onboarding, data entry, travel', 'Not specified', 1, 0, 'OFF', 'open', '2026-07-04 11:49:07', 'full_time', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL);
